%% 07 — Delivery timeline by epic
%% Drawn from: gh pr list --state merged (297 PRs into dev or a stack branch,
%%   2026-09-13 to 2026-10-29), each PR's closing issue and its "epic:" label,
%%   else the issue's parent, else the story tag in the title. 62 PRs with no
%%   epic anywhere are the last lane; #221's void stack, unlabelled, is under
%%   resolution. Releases are the [Release] PRs into main, named as their
%%   titles name them. The deploy row is outside that window: #19's five PRs,
%%   #603 to #607, merged into dev on 2026-11-01, and #613 took them to main the
%%   same day, as did the unrelated #597: neither is in the Releases lane, whose
%%   labels would collide. Staging (a #19 criterion, ADR 0026) and #20 have no
%%   target date, so they are a marker at the chart's end rather than a bar.
%% A bar runs from an epic's first merged PR to its last. It is a span, not
%% continuous work. FE bars are shaded (`active`), BE bars plain.
%% Compact mode shares a row between bars that do not overlap, which would pile
%% the release labels onto one row. Mermaid draws a milestone at the middle of
%% its span, so each release is given a span centred on its merge date
%% (4, 17, 19, 20, 24 and 29 Oct), sized so that overlapping spans put labels
%% that would collide on different rows (Mermaid fills rows in source order,
%% hence #577 before #504). The span itself is not drawn. "It." is Iteration,
%% as the release PRs' titles name them.
%%{init: {"gantt": {"displayMode": "compact", "barHeight": 18, "barGap": 4}, "themeCSS": ".tick text { font-size: 15px; } .sectionTitle { font-size: 15px; } .taskText, .taskTextOutsideRight, .taskTextOutsideLeft { font-size: 14.5px; }"}}%%
